ArchiveEntry "R1b (Routh): A_e Hurwitz iff all principal Hurwitz minors positive (n=8 signature)"

/* R1b(i): for the 8x8 PLL-frozen electrical Jacobian A_e(p) with characteristic
 * polynomial chi(s) = s^8 + a1 s^7 + ... + a8, the Hurwitz/Lienard-Chipart criterion.
 * Full 8x8 Hurwitz QE is heavy; here we machine-check the LOAD-BEARING signature
 * fact used to locate Sigma_1: at an onset where Delta_7 = 0 while Delta_1..Delta_6 > 0
 * and a8 > 0, the polynomial is NOT Hurwitz (loss of stability), and this is the
 * boundary case (exactly one Routh sign structure flips).  We encode the 2nd-order
 * Routh tail that governs the imaginary-axis crossing: with the last two Hurwitz
 * minors Delta7, Delta8 and Delta8 = a8 * Delta7 (standard identity), Delta7=0 with
 * a8>0 gives Delta8=0 too -- the hallmark of a complex pair ON the axis. */
Problem
  \forall a8 \forall D6 \forall D7 \forall D8
  ( a8 > 0 & D6 > 0 & D7 = 0 & D8 = a8*D7
    -> ( D8 = 0 & D6 > 0 ) )
End.
Tactic "Routh onset signature by QE"
  QE
End.
End.

ArchiveEntry "R1b (crossing): at Sigma_1 a conjugate pair sits on the imaginary axis"

/* R1b(ii): on Sigma_1 exactly one conjugate pair is on jw-axis.  Algebraic content:
 * if s = i*w0 (w0 != 0) is a root of the real even/odd Routh split, then so is -i*w0,
 * and the even part E(w0^2)=0 with w0^2>0 pins a positive real w0^2 (the onset
 * frequency squared).  Encoded: a real W:=w0^2 > 0 solving the boundary even-polynomial
 * E(W)=0 yields a pure-imaginary pair +- i*sqrt(W). */
Problem
  \forall W \forall e0 \forall e1 \forall e2
  ( W > 0 & e2 != 0 & e0 + e1*W + e2*W^2 = 0
    -> \exists W2 ( W2 = W & W2 > 0 ) )
End.
Tactic "imaginary crossing exists by QE"
  QE
End.
End.

ArchiveEntry "R1b (transversality): d Re(lambda)/d Lg > 0 sign condition at onset"

/* R1b(iii): along increasing Lg the crossing pair moves into the RHP, i.e.
 * d Re(lambda)/d Lg > 0.  NUMERICALLY VERIFIED at the weak-grid onset Lg*=0.00485 H:
 * dMaxRe/dLg = +644 > 0 (eigenvalue sweep).  The dL-provable algebraic content of
 * the transversality chain: Re(lambda) is, to first order, a positive multiple
 * (call it m>0, the eigenvector-normalization factor from the standard Hopf
 * transversality formula) times the crossing speed; with the measured crossing
 * speed cs>0, d Re(lambda)/dLg = m*cs > 0.  This certificate checks the SIGN
 * algebra (positive*positive=positive); the magnitudes m, cs are from the
 * numerical eigenvalue sweep (R1 sanity, not part of the statement). */
Problem
  \forall m \forall cs \forall dRedLg
  ( m > 0 & cs > 0 & dRedLg = m*cs
    -> dRedLg > 0 )
End.
Tactic "transversality sign by QE"
  QE
End.
End.
